  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.02772v2</id>
    <title>Self-Evolutionary Replanning for Failure-Aware Motion Planning</title>
    <updated>2026-09-26T12:40:25Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.02772v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.02772v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Motion planners tuned under nominal conditions can fail when execution conditions change. Existing differentiable adaptation methods provide efficient online updates but remain constrained by static loss functions and gradient-only parameter updates. We propose Self-Evolutionary RePlanning (SERP), a failure-aware framework that jointly adapts motion-planner parameters and loss function weights from closed-loop execution feedback. SERP provides two adaptation mechanisms. First, in-context learning with auto-differentiation (ILAD) enables rapid online adaptation by coupling local numerical refinement with history-conditioned semantic intervention. Auto-differentiation performs numerical updates, while a vision-language model (VLM) interprets recent adaptation history to jointly revise planner parameters and loss weights when local adaptation becomes ineffective. Second, the memory-augmented rollout system (MARS) extends ILAD into a deliberative and evolutionary recovery process with memory-guided candidate generation and parallel low-fidelity rollout evaluation. The resulting recovery trace is then consolidated into recovery memory to guide future adaptation. Extensive simulation and real-world experiments demonstrate improved failure recovery performance over various baselines across diverse environments.</summary>
    <category term="cs.RO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-03-03T09:12:29Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>8 pages, 9 figures, 4 tables, submitted to IEEE for possible publication</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.RO"/>
    <author>
      <name>Guoliang Li</name>
    </author>
